@Tripora.UserService_HostAddress = http://localhost:5001

### ======================================================
### REGISTRATION SCENARIOS
### ======================================================

### Registration Scenario 1 & 5: Valid Customer Registration
POST {{Tripora.UserService_HostAddress}}/api/users/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Eleanor Vance",
  "email": "eleanor.vance@tripora.com",
  "password": "SecurePassword123!",
  "confirmPassword": "SecurePassword123!"
}

###

### Registration Scenario 2: Duplicate Email
POST {{Tripora.UserService_HostAddress}}/api/users/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Eleanor Vance",
  "email": "eleanor.vance@tripora.com",
  "password": "AnotherPassword123!",
  "confirmPassword": "AnotherPassword123!"
}

###

### ======================================================
### LOGIN & JWT AUTHENTICATION SCENARIOS
### ======================================================

### Login Scenario 1 & 3: Successful Login (Generates JWT Token)
# @name login
POST {{Tripora.UserService_HostAddress}}/api/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "eleanor.vance@tripora.com",
  "password": "SecurePassword123!"
}

###

### Extract Auth Token from response
@authToken = {{login.response.body.data.token}}

### Login Scenario 2A: Invalid Password
POST {{Tripora.UserService_HostAddress}}/api/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "eleanor.vance@tripora.com",
  "password": "WrongPassword999!"
}

###

### Login Scenario 2B: Account Does Not Exist
POST {{Tripora.UserService_HostAddress}}/api/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "unregistered.user@tripora.com",
  "password": "SecurePassword123!"
}

###

### Login Scenario 4: Access Protected Resource With Valid JWT Token
GET {{Tripora.UserService_HostAddress}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

### Login Scenario 5: Unauthorized Access Denied (Without Token)
GET {{Tripora.UserService_HostAddress}}/api/users/me
Accept: application/json

###
